<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="tour-detail-layout">
  <div class="tour-detail-main reveal">
    <h2>Tour Overview</h2>
    <p>Three countries, three distinct Silk Road cultures, one seamless journey. From the architectural splendor of Uzbekistan's Timurid empire to the pristine alpine lakes and nomadic traditions of Kyrgyzstan, and finally the vibrant crossroads of Kashgar in China's Xinjiang — this 20-day tour weaves together the most fascinating chapters of the ancient Silk Road.</p>

    <div class="highlight-box"><h3>Trip Highlights</h3><ul>
      <li>Registan Square at sunset — Samarkand's crown jewel</li><li>Bukhara's thousand-year-old trading domes</li>
      <li>Khiva's perfectly preserved walled city</li>
      <li>Issyk-Kul Lake — the "Pearl of the Tianshan"</li>
      <li>Eagle hunting demonstration with Kyrgyz nomads</li>
      <li>Song-Kul Lake yurt stay at 3,000m</li>
      <li>Torugart Pass border crossing into China</li>
      <li>Kashgar Sunday Bazaar — the ultimate Silk Road market</li>
    </ul></div>

    <h2>Day-by-Day Itinerary</h2>
    <ul class="itinerary">
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>1</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Arrive in Tashkent, Uzbekistan</h4><p>Welcome to Uzbekistan. Airport transfer, check into your hotel. Evening orientation walk through Amir Timur Square. Welcome dinner with traditional plov and Uzbek bread (non).</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Tashkent 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>2</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Tashkent — Capital of Central Asia</h4><p>Visit Khast Imam Complex, home to the 7th-century Uthman Quran. Explore Chorsu Bazaar's domed halls. Afternoon at the State Museum of History and Navoi Opera Square.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Tashkent 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>3</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Tashkent &#8594; Samarkand (High-speed train)</h4><p>Afrosiyob train to Samarkand (2 hrs). First glimpse of Registan Square in the golden afternoon light. Visit Gur-e-Amir, Timur's magnificent mausoleum that inspired the Taj Mahal.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Samarkand 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>4</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Samarkand — The Rome of the East</h4><p>Full day exploring Timur's capital. Bibi-Khanym Mosque, Shah-i-Zinda necropolis, Ulugbek's 15th-century observatory. Afternoon at Konigil village for traditional silk paper-making.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Samarkand 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>5</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Samarkand &#8594; Bukhara</h4><p>Morning drive across the Kyzylkum Desert to Bukhara (4 hrs). Afternoon: walk through Lyabi-Hauz, the 17th-century plaza of pools and mulberry trees. Sunset from the Ark Fortress walls.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Bukhara 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>6</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Bukhara — City of 1,001 Domes</h4><p>Kalon Minaret (so beautiful Genghis Khan spared it), the trading domes, Chor Minor, and a carpet-weaving masterclass. Evening folklore show at Nadir Divan-Begi Madrasah.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Bukhara 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>7</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Bukhara &#8594; Khiva (Kyzylkum Desert crossing)</h4><p>Scenic drive across the Red Sand Desert to Khiva (7 hrs). Arrive at golden hour when the mud-brick walls of Itchan Kala glow. Rooftop dinner overlooking the minarets.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Khiva 3&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>8</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Khiva — The Open-Air Museum</h4><p>Explore Itchan Kala's maze of madrasahs, mosques, and minarets. Climb the unfinished Kalta Minor Minaret. Visit the stone courtyard where slaves were once traded on the Silk Road.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Khiva 3&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>9</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Khiva &#8594; Urgench &#9992; Tashkent &#8594; Bishkek</h4><p>Morning drive to Urgench Airport. Fly to Tashkent, connect to Bishkek, Kyrgyzstan. Evening stroll through Ala-Too Square. Try traditional Kyrgyz dishes at a local restaurant.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Bishkek 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>10</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Bishkek &#8594; Ala Archa National Park</h4><p>Day trip to Ala Archa National Park (40 mins from Bishkek). Hike through juniper forests to a waterfall with views of 4,800m peaks. Afternoon: Osh Bazaar and Burana Tower.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Bishkek 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>11</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Bishkek &#8594; Issyk-Kul Lake</h4><p>Drive to Issyk-Kul, the world's second-largest alpine lake (4 hrs). Visit the petroglyphs at Cholpon-Ata — 2,000-year-old stone carvings. Afternoon: swim in the lake or hike along the shore.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Issyk-Kul Resort</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>12</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Issyk-Kul — Karakol & Jeti-Oguz</h4><p>Drive along the southern shore to Karakol. Visit the wooden Dungan Mosque and Orthodox Church. Afternoon at Jeti-Oguz — the "Seven Bulls" red rock formations. Overnight in a yurt camp.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#9968;&#65039; Yurt Camp</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>13</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Jeti-Oguz &#8594; Song-Kul Lake</h4><p>Long but spectacular drive to Song-Kul Lake (3,016m). Arrive at this high-altitude jewel surrounded by snow-capped peaks. Stay in a traditional yurt with a Kyrgyz nomad family. Evening: stargazing at 3,000m.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#9968;&#65039; Song-Kul Yurt</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>14</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Song-Kul — Nomad Life & Eagle Hunting</h4><p>Rise with the sun over the lake. Ride horses across the jailoo (summer pasture). Watch an eagle hunting demonstration — a tradition passed down through generations of Kyrgyz nomads. Help milk mares for kumis.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#9968;&#65039; Song-Kul Yurt</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>15</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Song-Kul &#8594; Naryn</h4><p>Descend from the high pasture to Naryn, Kyrgyzstan's longest river source. Visit the 15th-century Tash Rabat caravanserai — a perfectly preserved stone inn where Silk Road traders once sheltered.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Naryn Guesthouse</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>16</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Naryn &#8594; Torugart Pass &#8594; Kashgar, China!</h4><p>Early start to cross Torugart Pass (3,752m) — the high-altitude border between Kyrgyzstan and China. Clear customs, descend into Xinjiang. Arrive in Kashgar for a well-earned rest.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Kashgar 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>17</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar — Sunday Bazaar & Old City</h4><p>If Sunday: the legendary bazaar — livestock, spices, carpets, everything. Explore the Old City's maze of adobe alleyways. Evening tea at a 100-year-old teahouse with live Uyghur music.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Kashgar 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>18</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar — Karakoram Highway to Karakul Lake</h4><p>Drive the legendary Karakoram Highway to Karakul Lake (3,600m). Stand in awe before Muztagh Ata (7,546m) reflected in the lake's mirror surface. Visit Kyrgyz nomad settlements along the way.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Kashgar 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>19</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Kashgar — Id Kah Mosque & Farewell</h4><p>Visit Id Kah Mosque, China's largest. Explore Abakh Khoja Tomb, the "Fragrant Concubine's" mausoleum. Farewell dinner — a grand Uyghur feast with music and dance.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127976; Kashgar 4&#9733;</span><span>&#127860; B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>20</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Depart Kashgar</h4><p>Airport transfer. Your tri-country Silk Road odyssey concludes. You've followed in the footsteps of Marco Polo. &#20877;&#35265;!</p><div class="day-meta"><span>&#127860; B</span></div></div></li>
    </ul>

